; atleastw_length_mismatch_beats_sample_mode: the vecs are compared before
; the model register is discriminated.
;
; The ATLEAST case one directory over, on the other half of the same
; ordering: exec_at_least_w resolves both vec operands and compares their
; lengths before it reaches the register, so a sample in r0 with mismatched
; vecs raises VecLengthMismatch. xqvm_py checked the mode first and raised
; XqmxMode, which is a rule that had not fired yet on the other VM.
;
; ISA.md's ATLEASTW row says "both implementations raise VecLengthMismatch
; otherwise". This vector is what holds it to that unconditionally, rather
; than only when the model register already holds a model.

PUSH 4
BSMX r0          ; a sample, not a model

VEC r2
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2       ; indices has 1 entry

VEC r3           ; coeffs has 0

PUSH 0           ; k
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ATLEASTW r0 r2 r3
HALT
